[38;5;231m⏺[39m I'll sketch this in a browser tab so it's easier to see. It's opening now at
  [94m]8;id=lbb2fr;http://localhost:59870/?key=05db91ba037a7842d5f49d530166f57ee73f05a82420b917c360bdab117d5f00\http://localhost:59870/?key=05db91ba037a7842d5f49d530166f57ee73f05a82420b917c360bdab117d5f00[39m]8;;\ (it's token-intensive, so
  say the word if you'd rather keep things in the terminal).

  The screen shows three placements. All three use the same controls:
  - A quick view: All events / Failed sign-ins / Security changes.
  - An event type Select.
  - A From/To date range for picking a week.

  The placements:
  - [1mA: one filter bar above the table.[0m Everything is visible in one panel.
  - [1mB: quick views in their own row, with type and dates in a quieter row below.[0m "Failed sign-ins" is the first thing
    people see.
  - [1mC: a "Filter" button that opens a popover, with active filters shown as removable tags.[0m It's the most compact, but
    failed sign-ins is one click further away.

  I lean toward [1mB[0m. It puts your two most common needs one click from the top, and picking a week stays available
  underneath. Have a look and tell me what you think here. You can also click an option in the browser.

  The companion saves its files in [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m in the repo, and that folder isn't in [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m yet. You may want to
  add it so it never ends up in a commit.

